<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Shailodbhava dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">550 CE – 736 CE (approx.) · capital Kongoda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of coastal Odisha ruling the land of Kongoda, linked to some of the earliest surviving temples of Bhubaneswar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Shailodbhavas, whose name means born of the rock, ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kongoda">Kongoda</a>, the coastal region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganjam-district">Ganjam</a> and Puri, from the 6th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhavaraja-ii">Madhavaraja II</a> began as a feudatory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shashanka">Shashanka</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gauda-kingdom">Gauda Kingdom</a> and asserted independence after Shashanka's death.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty is known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a>, which describe a legendary origin from a rock and record land given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a>. The kings were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivas</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parashurameshvara-temple">Parashurameshvara temple</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar">Bhubaneswar</a>, one of the oldest surviving temples of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kalinga">Kalinga</a> style, is generally dated to their time. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> described <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kongoda">Kongoda</a> as a strong kingdom with good harbours.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the first half of the 8th century the Shailodbhavas were displaced by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhauma-kara-dynasty">Bhauma-Kara dynasty</a>, which unified much of coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 550 CE – 736 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:70.65%;width:3.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>550 CE – 736 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kongoda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Madhavaraja II, Dharmaraja</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shaivism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shailodbhavas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=643&amp;focus=shailodbhava-dynasty" aria-label="Shailodbhava dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6823 1301 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Shailodbhava dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7143 1557h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7143 1557h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=643&amp;focus=shailodbhava-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
